  message: "Closed by PR #2342 (dev 2bc49faef). REPRO RE-RUN on dev, 2026-11-22 ~23:35Z: the item's own fixture (fast_smart_test_build_11172026/audit/probe4_electron, copied to /tmp/pahom_fx; `hypergumbo run /tmp/pahom_fx --no-sketch-fan-out --no-handler-slices`, exit 0): the line `ipcMain.handle('ping', () => 'pong');` (repo/main.js:7) now gives the entry `event_handler` \"Electron IPC handler\" on the handler symbol `_cb_handle`, which carries the concept ipc_handler from electron.yaml; before, the entry list of that fixture held electron_main, electron_preload and script_module only. HOW: the JavaScript analyzer records a usage context for a call that hands a local function to a library when a usage row names the call at that argument (framework_patterns.usage_row_names_call); electron.yaml's new rows name ipcMain on / once / handle / handleOnce and ipcRenderer on / once. The IPC linker also writes dispatches_to from each ipc:receive:<channel> node to its handler now. Measured on real code by the work package (workadventure desktop/electron): 13 IPC handler entries, 13 channel -> handler edges. NOT COVERED, filed in WI-rikum: an import-aliased receiver (`ipcMain as ipc`; session-desktop has 29 such sites), a handler that is an object property with no symbol. The IPC linker still reads comments (WI-pisur, reproduced during the triage)."  # 2e8c
